  "question": {
    "text": "The amount of work done to break a big water drop of radius ' $R$ ' into 27 small drops of equal radius is 10 J . The work done required to break the same big drop into 64 small drops of equal radius will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Ml2vb",
      "text": "15 J",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "rzaey",
      "text": "5 J",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "sZZnY",
      "text": "20 J",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "S1rHi",
      "text": "10 J",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& W_1=s 4 \\pi\\left(\\frac{R}{3}\\right)^2 \\times 27-4 \\pi R^2 \\cdot s \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow W_1=4 \\pi R^2 \\cdot s(2)=10 \\text { Joule }\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nNow, $W_2=s 4 \\pi R^2(4-1)=4 \\pi R^2 s \\times 3$\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad W_2=3 \\times \\frac{10}{2}=15 \\text { Joule }$",
    "image": null
  },
